§ `s 3(1)-(4) -- can I be appointed a notary public`

#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be appointed a notary public` `a practising lawyer of 10 years, found fit, Council consulted`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to be appointed a notary public` `a practising lawyer of exactly 7 years`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible to be appointed a notary public` `a practising lawyer of 6 years`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible to be appointed a notary public` `a lawyer of 20 years no longer practising`

#ASSERT `Can I be appointed a notary public` `a practising lawyer of 10 years, found fit, Council consulted` EQUALS `yes, if the Senate chooses: it has absolute discretion and there is no appeal from its decision`
#ASSERT `Can I be appointed a notary public` `a practising lawyer of exactly 7 years` EQUALS `yes, if the Senate chooses: it has absolute discretion and there is no appeal from its decision`
#ASSERT `Can I be appointed a notary public` `a practising lawyer of 6 years` EQUALS `no: section 3(2) requires not less than 7 years in practice`
#ASSERT `Can I be appointed a notary public` `a lawyer of 20 years no longer practising` EQUALS `no: section 3(2) requires a practising advocate and solicitor in Singapore`
#ASSERT `Can I be appointed a notary public` `a practising lawyer of 12 years the Senate does not find fit` EQUALS `no: section 3(1) appoints only persons the Senate finds fit and proper`
#ASSERT `Can I be appointed a notary public` `a practising lawyer of 10 years, Council not consulted` EQUALS `not until the Senate has consulted the Council of the Law Society, as section 3(3) requires`
#ASSERT `Can I be appointed a notary public` `a practising lawyer of 10 years seeking 13 months` EQUALS `no: an appointment may not be for more than 12 months`

#ASSERT NOT `Can I appeal against the Senate's decision on my appointment`

§ `s 3(5), (6) -- can I be appointed temporarily`

#ASSERT `Can I be appointed a notary public temporarily` `a practising lawyer of 6 years` EQUALS `yes, if the Senate chooses: it has absolute discretion and there is no appeal from its decision`
#ASSERT `Can I be appointed a notary public temporarily` `a practising lawyer of 12 years the Senate does not find fit` EQUALS `yes, if the Senate chooses: it has absolute discretion and there is no appeal from its decision`
#ASSERT `Can I be appointed a notary public temporarily` `a lawyer of 20 years no longer practising` EQUALS `no: section 3(5) requires a practising advocate and solicitor in Singapore`
#ASSERT `Can I be appointed a notary public temporarily` `a practising lawyer of 10 years, Council not consulted` EQUALS `not until the Senate has consulted the Council of the Law Society, as section 3(3) requires`
#ASSERT `Can I be appointed a notary public temporarily` `a practising lawyer of 10 years seeking 13 months` EQUALS `no: an appointment may not be for more than 12 months`
#ASSERT `Can I be appointed a notary public temporarily` `a practising lawyer of 2 years, no notary about to be away` EQUALS `no: section 3(5) applies only while a notary public is about to be absent from Singapore for more than one month`

