§ `s 4 -- what may I do with an affidavit or statutory declaration`

#ASSERT `May I administer the oath for, take or attest the affidavit` `an affidavit for a Singapore court` EQUALS `no: section 4(2) takes it out of my powers, because it is to be used in a court or place within Singapore`
#ASSERT `May I administer the oath for, take or attest the affidavit` `an affidavit for a Malaysian court` EQUALS `yes, under section 4(3)(a)(iii): it is to be used in a court or place outside Singapore`
#ASSERT `May I administer the oath for, take or attest the affidavit` `an affidavit proving due execution, for use in Singapore` EQUALS `yes, under section 4(3)(a)(i): it confirms or proves the due execution of a document`
#ASSERT `May I administer the oath for, take or attest the affidavit` `a crew member's affidavit about the vessel, for a Singapore court` EQUALS `yes, under section 4(3)(a)(ii): it is sworn by a vessel's master or crew member about the vessel`
#ASSERT `May I administer the oath for, take or attest the affidavit` `a statutory declaration with no stated place of use` EQUALS `not covered by this encoding: it turns on English notarial practice (section 4(1)) or prescribed powers (section 4(3)(c))`

§ `s 5 -- must my appointment be revoked`

#ASSERT `Must my appointment be revoked` `I have become a bankrupt` EQUALS `it must be revoked under section 5(a), if it so appears to the Senate, by order published in the Gazette`
#ASSERT `Must my appointment be revoked` `I have made an arrangement with my creditors` EQUALS `it must be revoked under section 5(a), if it so appears to the Senate, by order published in the Gazette`
#ASSERT `Must my appointment be revoked` `I have been struck off` EQUALS `it must be revoked under section 5(b), if it so appears to the Senate, by order published in the Gazette`
#ASSERT `Must my appointment be revoked` `misconduct the Senate thinks makes me unfit` EQUALS `it must be revoked under section 5(c), by order published in the Gazette`
#ASSERT `Must my appointment be revoked` `misconduct the Senate does not think makes me unfit` EQUALS `section 5 does not require it to be revoked`
#ASSERT `Must my appointment be revoked` `I have stopped practising` EQUALS `section 5 does not require it to be revoked`
#ASSERT `Must my appointment be revoked` `nothing has happened` EQUALS `section 5 does not require it to be revoked`

§ `s 6 -- revocation at my own request`

#ASSERT `Can I have my appointment revoked at my own request` TRUE EQUALS `the Senate may revoke my appointment by notification in the Gazette, but need not`
#ASSERT `Can I have my appointment revoked at my own request` FALSE EQUALS `section 6 does not apply unless I request revocation`

